  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Predictive Maintenance & Asset Health for a complex refinery running 20 critical assets across crude, FCC, hydrotreating, reforming, and alkylation. Stakeholders include the Reliability VP (availability, MTBF/MTTR, predictive catch rate), Refinery Manager (throughput loss from unplanned events), and Turnaround/Maintenance leads (RUL-driven scoping for the next TAR).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Availability = availability_pct; Solomon top-quartile refiners hold >96%; second-quartile ~93-96%\n- MTBF = mtbf_days (higher is better); rotating equipment industry target >180 days, fixed equipment >365 days\n- MTTR = mttr_hours; world-class refiners restore critical rotating equipment in <8 hours\n- Predicted RUL = predicted_rul_days on sensor_readings; <30 days is a planning trigger for intervention\n- Predictive catch rate = was_predicted = TRUE share of total events; mature programs target >50%\n- Throughput loss = throughput_loss_bbl on maintenance_events; converted at refining margin to lost-margin $\n- Alert escalation = alert_level in ('Alarm','Trip'); Trip events typically force unit rate cut or shutdown\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - sensor_readings_metrics (source: sensor_readings) — dims: reading_timestamp, equipment_id, equipment_type, process_unit, alert_level; measures: avg_health_score, total_readings, alarm_trip_count, min_rul_days, total_sensor_value, max_sensor_value.\n  - maintenance_events_metrics (source: maintenance_events) — dims: event_date, equipment_id, equipment_type, process_unit, event_type, failure_mode, was_predicted; measures: total_events, total_downtime_hours, total_throughput_loss_bbl, total_repair_cost_usd, avg_repair_cost_usd, max_downtime_hours.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. equipment_name, sensor_value, predicted_rul_days at row level, repair_cost_usd at row level, availability_pct from equipment_health_monthly).\n- For \"process unit health score\" questions, use the monthly snapshot `equipment_health_monthly` (one row per unit per month), not `sensor_readings_metrics` (per-reading rollup that returns extra rows).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset",
    "What is the current asset composition by equipment type and process unit, and the average health score and availability of each?",
    "Which equipment has predicted remaining useful life under 30 days and the worst MTBF, making it the top intervention priority?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the highest sensor value for each reading timestamp?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_timestamp, MEASURE(max_sensor_value) AS max_sensor_value",
        "FROM {fqn}.sensor_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY max_sensor_value DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Rank reading timestamps by total sensor value",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_timestamp, MEASURE(total_sensor_value) AS total_sensor_value",
        "FROM {fqn}.sensor_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY total_sensor_value DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average equipment downtime in hours trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, AVG(downtime_hours) AS avg_downtime_hours",
        "FROM {fqn}.maintenance_events",
        "GROUP BY event_date",
        "ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total raw sensor measurement value over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_timestamp, SUM(sensor_value) AS total_sensor_value",
        "FROM {fqn}.sensor_readings",
        "GROUP BY reading_timestamp ORDER BY reading_timestamp"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total equipment downtime in hours over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, SUM(downtime_hours) AS total_downtime_hours",
        "FROM {fqn}.maintenance_events",
        "GROUP BY event_date ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average average health score for the month changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_month, AVG(avg_health_score) AS avg_avg_health_score",
        "FROM {fqn}.equipment_health_monthly",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_month ORDER BY snapshot_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How does lowest remaining useful life days compare across equipments?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_timestamp, MEASURE(min_rul_days) AS min_rul_days",
        "FROM {fqn}.sensor_readings_metrics",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY min_rul_days DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    }
  ],
